USER.append(('Define table and column business meanings', ['A data dictionary explains what a table or column means to the people using the application. DPH captures technical SQL structure, but a knowledgeable contributor must supply business meanings. Open Database schema in the upper-right page selector. Select a declared table or column. The labeled details area starts with its saved business dictionary, or explains that none has been recorded for these captured source bytes.', 'Scroll the command strip horizontally to the right and click Edit dictionary. Enter the named contributor, Business definition, Business owner or steward, Sensitivity and handling, and Evidence and remaining unknowns. These fields are required; explicitly write Unknown and the person or evidence needed when an answer is unavailable. Units values and business usage is optional. Do not paste actual customer records, credentials or confidential example values. A sensitivity entry is documentation, not automatic access control.', 'The editor begins with business fields. Scroll downward to inspect the read-only schema identity, source path, SHA256, original capture generation, object kind/name, owning table and statement line. These identify the exact captured declaration; duplicate table names are not merged. DPH does not infer a business definition, responsible owner or sensitivity from an SQL name or declared type.', 'Click Apply to Knowledge draft. The editor closes and Knowledge displays the protected structured draft. Click Save to create an immutable revision. Apply alone does not persist anything. Use Discard edit if you do not want the draft. To change a saved definition, return to Database schema, select the same table or column and click Edit dictionary again. Editing requires a fresh human review.', 'Click Open dictionary history beside Edit dictionary to view contributor, editor, review state and immutable revisions in Knowledge. Enter the named reviewer and choose Verify review, Reject or Retire as appropriate. Saving a definition does not verify its truth. Additional canonical source, relationship, screenshot or section evidence can be added on Knowledge links. Open source on Database schema follows the selected captured source under the existing hash checks.', 'The Database schema text filter also searches saved current definitions, owners, sensitivity and usage. Clear the filter to restore the inventory. Tables or columns not captured as supported declarations cannot be given invented schema identities. A changed SQL resource does not automatically inherit its old dictionary. When the same source/record/name has historical text, details explains the mismatch and Open dictionary history preserves access. Other unmatched records remain in Knowledge. Recheck business facts and author a definition for the newly captured declaration.', 'Project handoffs include matching attributed dictionary records through the existing Knowledge sections and structured canonical records. Source exclusions and selected source scope apply; definitions whose captured source hashes differ are omitted. Review business descriptions before publishing. Native controls remain editable in the Delphi IDE. No SQL, target application or database server is run by this workflow.']))
ENGINEERING.append(('Maintain attributed schema dictionaries', ['TDPHDatabaseSchema provides NewDictionary, ValidateDictionary, DictionaryIdentity, DictionaryTitle, DictionaryBody and FindDictionary in the existing schema unit. A data_dictionary record contains fourteen bounded text fields. Its captured anchor retains the exact schema record ID, source SHA256, original capture generation, kind, name, owning table and statement line. Authored fields hold business definition, owner or steward, sensitivity/handling, evidence/unknowns and optional units/usage. Validation requires explicit content for the first four authored fields; Unknown is a legitimate attributed answer, not an inferred fact.', 'DPH.UI.DatabaseDictionary.pas and its FMX resource define a native structured editor. All labels, memo rows, dimensions, read-only states and Apply/Cancel controls are serialized and editable in the Object Inspector. Business fields appear first, captured identity below. DPH.UI.Main reuses the existing Knowledge draft/save flow, contributor, immutable revision history, optimistic revision checks, pending review and rejection/retirement commands. No new helper unit, runtime controls or database migration is introduced.', 'SaveKnowledge validates new anchors against the selected persisted workspace using the captured schema inventory. Forged object names or source lines are rejected. Scope, title, deterministic rendered body and target identity cannot be altered on an existing record. One dictionary per captured anchor is enforced, including retired records. Changes create a fresh needs_review revision. Contributor, editor and reviewer remain independent. Applying the native editor only prepares a draft and requires an explicit Save.', 'Database schema details show business meaning before captured technical facts. Its filter searches current authored dictionary bodies. Exact captured bytes are required for current lookup; old hash matches are reported as historical rather than moved onto a new source version. Unmatched historical records remain accessible in Knowledge. DPH.Publish.Model filters dictionary sections by included source files and matching SHA256, preserving existing publication redaction and attributed review state. Publisher version DPH-LEARNING-9 invalidates prior publication fingerprints.', 'Run tools/build-database-dictionary.cmd elevated. Its fixed ignored bin/database-dictionary-validation fixture captures real SQL resources, persists the workspace, checks required fields/types/bounds, forged/duplicate anchors, immutable identities, conflicting body rejection, contributor/review/revision history, stale review, table/column separation, historical lookup, export exclusions/hash mismatch, native serialized controls, modal Apply-to-draft flow, search, history navigation, compact renders and SQLite reopening. No selected application or SQL executes. Run ER, publishing and glossary regressions plus tools/build-wp0.cmd for the actual application and FMX baseline.', 'The editor implements an attributed dictionary workflow, not automatic knowledge of business meaning. Sensitivity is descriptive text, not an authorization mechanism. The captured schema remains partial and does not establish live deployment, SQL validity, migration order or business correctness. Human review and the source evidence must qualify every business assertion.']))
