USER.append(('Follow dataset and screen field bindings', ['Open the project or cached database, then choose Database connections in the upper-right page selector. Choose bound control in the kind filter to find data-aware controls, persistent field for captured field components, or data source for the intermediary between a control and dataset. Clear the text filter before changing the kind if no rows appear. Field names and component paths are searchable.', 'Select a bound control. The labeled details memo begins with DATASET AND SCREEN BINDINGS and lists its captured DataSource and DataField references. Select Target via DataSource in the reference selector and click Follow reference to inspect the data source, then follow DataSet to its dataset and Connection to the captured connection. To go straight to a captured persistent field, select Target via DataField and click Follow reference. A field name can refer to a calculated or lookup field; it does not prove a live database column.', 'Select a persistent field to see its captured FieldName, FieldKind, Required, ReadOnly, Size and Precision when serialized. Its DataSet reference identifies the serialized owning dataset, and Used by references return to bound controls. Choose a reference in the selector before clicking Follow reference; use the horizontal toolbar scrollbar when the command is outside the visible area. The details memo scrolls independently.', 'For FMX TLinkControlToField, DPH recognizes the serialized DataSource, FieldName and Control properties. Follow DataSource to TBindSourceDB and DataSet, FieldName to a unique persistent field, or Control to the captured visual target. This explains stored component references without creating any target component or executing LiveBindings. General expression-based bindings, dynamically created fields, runtime assignments, uncaptured inherited values and missing external targets remain unknown.', 'Duplicate field declarations or ambiguous data-source targets are reported without choosing one. A missing persistent field remains unresolved even if a runtime dataset might create it. Native controls are editable in the IDE. Run and test directions are in docs/guides/Dataset_Bindings_Run_and_Test.txt. The screen-data inventory is evidence for the selected captured revision, not a live database connection or an assertion about production data.']))
ENGINEERING.append(('Resolve captured dataset and field bindings', ['TDPHDatabaseConnections.Inspect extends the existing captured form inventory with known persistent TField classes, data-aware control property signals, TBindSourceDB and visual controls explicitly referenced by serialized binding Control properties. Only required reference/configuration metadata enters the projection; captions, credentials and connection values retain existing redaction. The source and persisted workspace remain unchanged.', 'Persistent field DataSet ownership is derived from its exact serialized parent path and resolved only to a unique dataset. Explicit LookupDataSet references remain distinct from ownership. ResolveFields indexes captured IDs and dataset-scoped case-insensitive FieldName values, then joins resolved control DataSource or BindSource, intermediary DataSet and persistent field identity. Multiple fields, incomplete or competing chains receive no target ID. Fields absent from captured declarations are not invented. Every property link retains its original property line and byte range; binary form evidence has byte positions rather than invented text lines.', 'The existing Follow reference workflow navigates outgoing and reverse references, resets filters and finds exact IDs across 250-row pages. Serialized kind choices add bound control, persistent field and binding control target. Binding explanations and field metadata appear before lengthy engine qualifications. No runtime controls, helper unit, target component loading or storage migration was introduced. Existing engine derivation remains unchanged.', 'The installed RAD Studio Data.Bind.Components source and official TLinkControlToField documentation establish the published DataSource, FieldName and Control contract. Data.Bind.DBScope supplies TBindSourceDB. Support describes serialized lexical candidates; it does not evaluate LiveBindings expressions or instantiate the target. General expression/factory/runtime/inherited behavior remains qualified rather than promoted to confirmed static binding.', 'Run tools/build-dataset-bindings.cmd elevated for 92 checks. Real text/binary DFM and FMX fixtures cover VCL and FMX field chains, parent ownership, reverse links, duplicate fields, missing/nil sources, lookup datasets, exact property evidence, native kind/text filters, follow navigation, compact layout, SQLite reopening and unchanged source/catalog. Connection and engine regressions each pass 66 checks. tools/build-wp0.cmd builds the actual application and verifies FMX resource bindings. Fixtures use fixed ignored bin/dataset-bindings-validation.']))
